First Author: Seraphin
Title: Prediction of heart transplant rejection from routine pathology slides with self-supervised deep learning
Source number: 44  ￼

Very short summary: This multicentre German study evaluated self-supervised deep learning on routine endomyocardial biopsy slides to predict cellular heart-transplant rejection. Five key findings were: (1) 1,079 histopathology slides from 325 patients across four cohorts from three German transplant centres were analyzed; (2) the primary training cohort contained 393 slides from 107 patients, with three independent hold-out/external cohorts used for validation; (3) for binary rejection prediction, mean cross-validated AUROC was 0.849, and external AUROCs were 0.734, 0.729, and 0.716; (4) for ISHLT grade prediction, the model performed best for 0R and 2/3R, with weaker performance for 1R; and (5) the authors’ SSL-attention MIL approach outperformed the CRANE comparator on their cohorts and produced attention maps that highlighted plausible morphology. Figures 1–2 and Table 1 were directly used for this extraction.  ￼

